WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.030
During this global pandemic

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.740
the world, for the most part,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.570
has looked to the World Health
Organization for guidance.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.470
The World Health Organization launches

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:14.300
a collaborative project to
find a vaccine and treatments.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.890
The World Health Organization warning

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.150
young people they're not invincible.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.520
The World Health Organization
officially announced

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.040
that this is a global pandemic.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.460
Instead, it's found controversy.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.810
Where President Trump does
find fault in handling

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.340
the pandemic is the World
Health Organization.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.370
You know, right now, they're,

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.850
they're literally a pipe organ for China.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:37.940
That's the way I view it.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.230
He accused the body of being too trusting

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.040
of China's assertions that it
had the virus under control.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.970
They not only need to answer to the needs

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:49.060
of over 100 members states, but the whims

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.960
and politics of the
countries and organizations

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.820
that donate the lion's
share of their budget.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.610
This is the story of how the
WHO tried to please the world,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.403
and ended up losing its biggest backer.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.720
The World Health Organization
was founded in 1948

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.450
by the also newly formed United Nations.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.550
Czechoslovakia, Yugoslavia,
Denmark, Greece,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.860
Poland, Hungary, and many other nations

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.820
have benefited from WHO.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.690
Headquartered in Geneva, they were tasked

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.430
to mandate and coordinate health policy.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.830
The initial vision for the
World Health Organization

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:30.910
was not only to make it an
important agency focusing

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:34.770
on health issues, disease
issues, and disease outbreaks,

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.700
but to try to create a form
of international cooperation

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.830
and collaboration that would
bind the nations together.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.230
And in the coming decades,

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.870
the WHO has taken on a
dizzying amount of missions,

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.060
from world-altering ones, like
the eradication of smallpox,

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.892
and the identification of HIV,

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:53.730
to awareness campaigns,

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.170
like safe driving, suicide prevention,

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.302
and anti-smoking PSAs.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.230
Well, there are several main roles.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:06.030
So one is to, what they
call it's a normative role,

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:10.880
which means it sets
standards for medical matters

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.606
throughout the world.

00:02:12.606 --> 00:02:16.680
And it has an important role
in providing technical support

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.590
to low and middle income countries.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.970
In order to tackle all
of those initiatives,

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:26.400
the WHO has become an
incredibly complex organization.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.430
There are six regional
offices around the world,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:33.370
in Congo, Denmark, America,

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.010
India, Egypt, and the Philippines,

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.180
all of which report to the
headquarters in Geneva.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.020
Each of which has its
own mode of functioning,

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.470
bureaucratic staff, and the like.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.600
The balance of authority
between the regional offices

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.380
and the headquarters in Geneva has always

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.120
been slightly problematic,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:56.290
trying to get them all
reading from the same page

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.660
when they have different
regional constituencies.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.570
And within those regional constituencies

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.090
are 150 country offices.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.920
In order to run all of those offices

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.390
requires a great deal of money,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.380
originally in the form of
assessed contributions,

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.840
or dues, by the member states.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.330
Assessments were determined
by the overall GDP,

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.470
or economic strength of
that particular country,

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.540
and its population.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.050
There was some formula worked out.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.300
And that formula worked for a while.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.060
Member states paid their dues.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.720
The WHO provided guidance

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.670
for health issues around the world.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.420
But over the last three decades,

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.150
that amount of money declined,

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.980
and is now only about 20%
of its overall budget.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.600
Today, the WHO is mostly funded
by voluntary contributions

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.750
with the United States being by far

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.130
the highest paying contributor
followed by the organization

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:51.410
started by this guy.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.120
If anything kills over 10 million people

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.490
in the next few decades
it's most likely to be

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:02.060
a highly infectious
virus, rather than a war.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.950
And when and where the
WHO gets its money from

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.690
influences so much about what it can do.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.400
And the Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.122
can say through our
extra budgetary funding

00:04:13.122 --> 00:04:16.360
with so much invested in polio,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.990
no one can tell us not to do that,

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.230
and that has made the
WHO a very unbalanced

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.050
and complicated organization.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.670
That unbalanced and
complicated bureaucracy

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.120
has consistently been

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.400
one of the World Health
Organization's biggest criticisms.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.130
But they've also been criticized
for how they've reacted

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:37.369
to the past two major
epidemics before COVID-19.

00:04:37.369 --> 00:04:40.070
We've now seen another outbreak of SARS.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:42.180
Potentially, we've seen a cluster

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.370
and transmission of the SARS virus.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.690
In 2003 was SARS.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:50.290
The WHO was criticized for
over-reacting to the disease,

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.580
which only had 774 known deaths,

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.810
but ended up costing East Asian countries

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:59.590
over $20 billion in lost GDP.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:02.400
Hotels, tour agencies,
and travel companies

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.490
are reported to have suffered huge losses

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:05.530
during the outbreak.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.370
That led to an under-reaction
in the response

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.680
to the Ebola epidemic
in West Africa in 2014.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.320
The big decision before them,

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.427
whether to label this worst
ever Ebola outbreak a, quote,

00:05:16.427 --> 00:05:20.090
"public health emergency
of international concern."

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.340
It didn't get a grip on the situation.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:25.640
It delayed in calling this
public health emergency

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.600
of international concern.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.970
The head of the World Health
Organization, Margaret Chan,

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.850
she has experience, yeah,
dealing with the outbreaks,

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.270
like bird flu, like SARS.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.980
Shouldn't she have been
handling this better?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:42.470
And so it was a general
mess, which led to many

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:47.370
investigations afterwards
about the WHO's very slow

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.200
and inefficient and inadequate response.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.110
So with the over-reaction to SARS

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:55.670
and under-reaction to
Ebola, COVID-19 was a chance

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.630
for the WHO to finally get things right,

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:02.220
and initially, everyone seemed
happy with their performance.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.000
COVID-19 is a real threat.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.900
It is a real threat to
everyone on the planet.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.100
It took the WHO one
month to declare COVID-19

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.400
an international health emergency.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.820
Compare that to the four
months it took them to call

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:19.550
Ebola an international health emergency.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.780
And Trump, who originally praised China

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.620
and the WHO's response to the pandemic--

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.490
So far, I think China's been

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.510
trying to be, or at least
they seem to be trying to be

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.020
somewhat transparent with us.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.000
He later turned on a dime,

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.510
blaming not only China for the pandemic,

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.530
but the WHO as well.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.370
The WHO willingly took China's assurances

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.513
to face value, and they
took it just at face value,

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:48.190
and defended the actions
of the Chinese government,

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:53.090
even praising China for
its so-called transparency.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.360
I don't think so.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.900
This was partially a response

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:59.750
to the WHO Director General
Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus'

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.940
constant praise of China
during the pandemic.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.490
I will praise China again and again,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:10.690
because its actions
actually helped in reducing

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.760
the spread of coronavirus
to other countries.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.480
China, as well as critics

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.610
of Trump's administration,
say Trump shifted the blame

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.610
for domestic political reasons,

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.300
to divert attention from
his catastrophic failure

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.310
to address the crisis in America,

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.090
whether it be from initially
downplaying the virus--

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:33.250
In this big vast land of ours,
this great country of ours,

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.120
we have 240 cases.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.980
Most of those people are gonna be fine.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.450
To touting unproven treatments--

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:42.780
A drug called hydroxychloroquine,

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.913
and it's shown very encouraging,

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.630
very, very encouraging early results.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.850
I think it's gonna be, I
think it's gonna be great.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.530
All while the death rate in America

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.330
surpassed that of the rest of the world,

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.390
and even though there were accusations

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.650
that China has not been transparent

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:02.850
about their numbers of COVID-19,

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.820
Tedros and the WHO were presented

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.860
with an impossible decision.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.540
This is international health diplomacy.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:14.400
The WHO has no power of enforcement.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.570
They cannot dispatch a team
against a country's wishes.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:21.090
They're dependent on data
coming out of that country

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:24.210
with the presumption that
countries will cooperate.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.480
In no situation could the WHO

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.400
please both the U.S. and China,

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.880
and that resulted in Trump
taking punitive action.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.840
Today, I'm instructing
my administration to halt

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.490
funding of the World Health Organization

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.920
while a review is conducted to assess

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:46.213
mismanaging and covering up
the spread of the coronavirus.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:50.190
And remember that chart
for who funds the WHO?

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.780
It's not just a huge loss
for the organization,

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.540
but for poorer countries around the globe.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.900
Every one of the essential
functions in the WHO

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:02.950
would be immediately
challenged and threatened,

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.440
if not stopped.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.410
And while America has the CDC

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:09.340
to create their own guidelines
and best practices--

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:12.620
Countries in Africa and
other parts of the world

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.830
don't have those resources,
and are desperately dependent

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.090
upon the WHO to provide
equipment, information,

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:24.180
interventions, and now those
will be seriously challenged,

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.810
if not stopped, completely.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:26.730
So where does this leave

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.350
the World Health Organization right now?

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:32.610
Apparently, it's not up to them, but us.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.590
Reminded of a quote by Larry Gostin,

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.630
who is one of the
international health experts

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.810
that is very important within the WHO.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:42.077
He has said, "the world has gotten

00:09:42.077 --> 00:09:44.600
"the WHO that it deserves."

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.260
The world has created this organization,

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:47.640
with all its faults, flaws,

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.270
inconsistencies, and inefficiencies.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.680
Can the world wake up?

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:53.630
Can this crisis force the world to say

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:56.720
we really do need a well-functioning

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.000
and truly neutral world health body

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.800
that will not be beholden to
various financial interests

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.730
or political interests, and
that if crisis can come,

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.700
not only disaster, but
hope, and a new beginning,

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:09.823
will the world let it?

